Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790661599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790639999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The 2850 high was not followed by a trend bar: 1790035200000 is an inside bar and 1790121600000 closed 2684.16 below its open, leaving 1790639999999 162 points under the high.", "1787270400000 left a ~256-point upper tail (high 2771 vs close 2515.3), and the following 27 bars could not exceed 2680, showing repeated failure to hold new highs.", "The final four bars are near-doji small-range bars (2636.28-2740.42), a tight two-sided cluster at the trend extreme that fits a final-flag shape rather than trend resumption.", "Two earlier vertical spikes in this window (1787097600000, 1787270400000) were each followed by multi-week ranges, so a stall after the 2850 high is consistent with this window's prior behavior."], "evidence_for": ["Progression of higher swing highs and higher swing lows over the last 40 bars: lows 2357.18 (1788307200000), 2358.62 (1789430400000), 2436.87 (1789689600000) and 2633.31 (1790208000000).", "1789689600000-1789948800000 broke above the 27-bar range and above the prior 2771 spike high, with closes near the highs and acceptance above 2612.02.", "The last seven bars hold entirely above the 2612.02 breakout close and above the 2436.87 breakout-low; no bear bar has closed below a prior bull swing low.", "Buying continued after each consolidation: ranges following the 2293.8/2771 spike highs and after the 27-bar range were all resolved upward."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens at 2006.31 (1780272000000) and sells off to a 1368.42 low (1780704000000) on bars that close near their lows.", "Price then recovers into a long overlapping range around 1710-1975 (e.g. 1692.84 low at 1782000000000 to 1974.46 high at 1785110400000) that persists until 1787011200000.", "1787097600000 is a large bull trend bar (open 1916.51, high 2293.8, close 2252.16), followed by closes of 2326.32 (1787184000000) and 2515.3 with a 2771 high (1787270400000): a three-bar vertical bull spike.", "From 1787356800000 to 1789603200000 the market holds a 27-bar two-sided range between 2357.18 (1788307200000 low) and 2680 (1789084800000 high), repeatedly rejecting 2520-2557 and 2357-2400 with heavy body overlap.", "1789689600000-1789948800000 breaks above that range and above the 2771 spike high: closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9, 2775.61, with the 2850 high at 1789948800000.", "The new high lacks strong follow-through: 1790035200000 is an inside bar and 1790121600000 closes 2684.16 below its open.", "The last seven bars (1790035200000-1790553600000) are overlapping, with the final four trading 2636.28-2740.42 and 1790639999999 closing 2687.88, roughly mid-range and 162 below the 2850 high."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Multi-month bull swing from the 1368.42 low to the 2850 high, with successively higher swing lows (1512.91, 1533.12, 2357.18, 2436.87, 2633.31) across the supplied window.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Three-bar vertical bull spike following a long two-sided range: open 1916.51 to close 2252.16 (1787097600000), close 2326.32 (1787184000000), then a 2771 high with a 2515.3 close and a large upper tail (1787270400000).", "end_time_ms": 1787270400000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Twenty-seven-bar two-sided range after the spike: repeated highs 2520-2557 plus the 2680 spike high at 1789084800000, and repeated lows 2357-2400 with 2357.18 at 1788307200000 and 2358.62 at 1789430400000; no sustained close beyond either edge.", "end_time_ms": 1789603200000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Four-bar bull breakout above the 27-bar range and above the 2771 spike high, closing near highs at 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9 and 2775.61, with the 2850 high printed at 1789948800000.", "end_time_ms": 1789948800000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Tight seven-bar consolidation just under the 2850 high; the last four bars are small overlapping dojis traded between 2636.28 and 2740.42, with no close beyond the 2612.02 breakout close and final close 2687.88.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2786.81"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation: a close above 2786.81 and then 2850 on a trend bar with follow-through, and a higher low above 2633.31, would confirm resumption of the bull channel.", "A bear body closing below 2633.31 and then below the 2612.02 breakout close would suggest the breakout has failed and shift the read toward a trading range or transition-unclear.", "A close below 2436.87 would break the most recent bull swing low and question the always-in-long classification.", "Continued overlapping bars contained between 2633.31 and 2786.81 with no boundary close would keep the current read of a bull trend in a breakout-mode tight range."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790654399999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the window's dominant move is the 34-bar bull leg (+20.8%) from 2358.62 to 2850, and the pullback held above that leg's midpoint (low 2633.31 versus 2604.31). Read as a bull flag, the regime would be bull-trend rather than trading-range, and the current coil would be a continuation pause.", "The 2850 bar with a ~127-point upper tail followed by lower highs and a lower low at 2633.31 can also be read as an early bear channel or a buying-climax top, which would make the recent flat action distribution/transition rather than a neutral range.", "The range boundaries are fuzzier than single prices - the top has been rejected anywhere from 2695 to 2740.42 and the bottom from 2633.31 to 2650.74 - so the 'range' label describes a zone rather than a clean two-price envelope.", "A ~3% wide coil after a 21% leg is a judgement call for breakout mode; it could equally be described as simply quieter trending-range rotation."], "evidence_for": ["Since the 2850 high (46 bars), there is no new high and no sustained lower-low sequence; the structure is bounded and both the 2633.31 low and the 2695-2740 top zone have been tested repeatedly without acceptance beyond them.", "Bar overlap is high and ranges are small in the most recent 20 bars (7.68-53.70 versus 191.94 at the 2850 bar), with closes alternating between the upper and lower halves - two-sided range behavior rather than trending behavior.", "Neither the wide bear bar at 1790553600000 (2685.90 to 2650.74) nor the bull bars at 1790582400000 and 1790596800000 produced follow-through beyond one or two bars, and the lower highs since 2850 (2804.59, 2786.81, 2740.42, 2718.83) have not converted into a sustained bear channel.", "The last ~11 bars contract into an even narrower coil inside the range, which is the configuration in which a directional resolution has not yet occurred."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window spans 120 closed H4 bars, 1788926400000 to 1790654399999; window low 2358.62 (bar at 1789488000000), window high 2850 (bar at 1789977600000).", "The bar at 1789977600000 is the widest of the window (open 2658.81, low 2658.06, high 2850) with range 191.94 and close 2723.15, about 46% of its range, leaving a ~127-point upper tail.", "After that high, no bar traded above 2850 and successive highs stepped down: 2804.59 (1790020800000), 2786.81 (1790136000000), 2778.33 (1790121600000), 2740.42 (1790323200000), 2721.75 (1790337600000), 2718.83 (1790496000000).", "The prior advance from 2358.62 to 2850 (34 bars, about +20.8%) ran with higher highs and higher lows; the subsequent pullback stopped at 2633.31 (1790236800000), above the leg midpoint 2604.31.", "The last 20 bars have small, heavily overlapping ranges (individual ranges 7.68 to 53.70) versus 191.94 at the 2850 bar, and closes alternate between the upper and lower halves of their bars.", "Both sides of the recent structure are repeatedly tested without follow-through: highs 2699.39 (1790265600000), 2699.53 (1790294400000), 2709.21 (1790611200000) on the top side; lows 2633.31 (1790236800000), 2637 (1790568000000), 2636.28 (1790582400000), 2652.27 (last bar) on the bottom side.", "Last bar (1790640000000): open 2687.88, high 2691.87, low 2652.27, close 2663.59 - a bear body closing in the lower quarter of its range.", "The first 40 bars were a two-sided decline from the 2487.82/2520.68 area to 2358.62, containing a one-bar spike to 2680 (1789128000000) that failed and a push to 2609.02 (1789416000000) that also failed."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening two-sided decline of the window: from 2520.68 (1788940800000 high) down to 2358.62, interrupted by a one-bar spike high 2680 (1789128000000, close 2555.52) that was not followed and a push to 2609.02 (1789416000000, close 2514.07) that reversed the same bar.", "end_time_ms": 1789488000000, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1788926400000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Bull leg: 34 bars of higher highs and higher lows from the 2358.62 low (1789488000000) to the 2850 spike high (1789977600000); the ending bar closed near mid-range with a large upper tail.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Post-high range: after the 2850 high, price slid to 2633.31 (1790236800000) and has since oscillated with overlapping bars and repeated boundary tests; the top is a zone of highs from roughly 2695 to 2740.42 (1790323200000) and the bottom a zone around 2633-2650.", "end_time_ms": 1790640000000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790164800000, "upper_boundary": "2740.42"}, {"description": "Tight 11-bar coil nested inside the range: 2636.28 (1790582400000 low) to 2718.83 (1790496000000 high), small bar ranges, closes alternating between bar halves, and the final bar a bear bar closing near the coil low.", "end_time_ms": 1790640000000, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2636.28", "start_time_ms": 1790496000000, "upper_boundary": "2718.83"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["An H4 close above 2740.42 (1790323200000 high), especially with the next bar closing above it, would argue the range is resolving upward; acceptance above 2786.81 and then 2850 would restore a bull-trend read.", "An H4 close below 2633.31 (1790236800000 low) and 2636.28 (1790582400000 low) with follow-through would expand the structure downward and make a bear leg the stronger read, with the bull leg midpoint 2604.31 as the next structural reference.", "Continued overlapping bars holding inside 2636.28 to 2718.83 without consecutive trend bars keeps the range and breakout-mode read.", "A run of consecutive trend bars closing at their extremes with expanding ranges would mark an actual breakout out of the coil rather than a boundary test."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2684.76", "close_time_ms": 1790233199999, "high": "2689